let g:mksk_python = 'python'
let g:mksk_args = ['--port', get(g:, 'LMSH_PORT', 8080)]
"let g:mksk_toggle_key = '<M-m>'
" plan folder = the current directory when mksk starts. Override:
"let g:mksk_dir = '~/echo-home/Documents/mksk'
" plan opened at start = the most up-to-date mksk--<plan>--YYYY-MM-DD.md in the folder, else a zero plan. Override:
"let g:mksk_plan = 'db-migration'


map mksk1 : silent source ~/echo-home/.vim/mimd/mksk/mksk.lua<CR>
map mkski : exec 'Mksk --port '.get(g:, 'LMSH_PORT', 8080)<CR>
map mkskt : MkskToggle<CR>
map mkskd : MkskDiff<CR>
map mkskf : MkskFile<CR>
map mkskp : MkskReview<CR>
map mkskj : InetJoin mksk<CR>
map mkskl : InetLeave mksk<CR>
map mkskq : MkskQuit<CR>

"HELP:
"- mksk is the make-sketch planner, cloned from neos: it keeps mksk--<plan_name>--YYYY-MM-DD.md up to date with you
"  (format: ~/echo-home/Documents/specs/make-sketch.md): plan updates and questions, on your request. mksk1 loads and
"  opens it on the most up-to-date plan file in the current directory, else on a zero plan (it names it when the first
"  change is saved). :Mksk <plan> opens a named plan instead (a new name starts a new plan).
"- mksk opens in a tab of its own: the plan file on top; below it the chat (left), the raw LLM log (right) and, while
"  mksk is on the network, the IFACE pane (network traffic and decisions) right of the log. The plan pane follows the
"  plan (another plan, today's new file); mkskf goes to it. Closed panes come back on the next Alt-m.
"- Alt-m from anywhere (normal/insert/terminal) goes to the chat; in the chat, Alt-m or q (normal) goes back to the tab
"  you came from. In visual mode Alt-m attaches the selected lines (e.g. rows of the targets table: "weigh these").
"- Ask without typing in the chat: :MkskAsk <text>, or :'<,'>MkskAsk <text> to attach a range.
"- In the chat: Enter sends, Up/Down history, Ctrl-X interrupts the LLM, Ctrl-C cancels. Busy: plain text steers the
"  running request, !text steers now, +text queues a new request. When mksk needs your answer while you are in another
"  tab, it notifies you instead of pulling you back.
"- Nothing is written without you: edits are staged and shown as a diff. y applies, n drops, v opens saved | proposed side
"  by side (mkskd any time; q there comes back), any other text tells it what to change. Approved changes always go to
"  today's file (the first one of a day creates it from the newest); older files are never written. Suggestions: pick
"  numbers (1,3), all, none, w (skip them and go straight to the diff of what is staged), or answer in your own words;
"  Enter on an option line picks it.
"- Memory: the whole chat stays in its context from start to quit (mkskq, which also closes the tab); ===r forgets it.
"  ===s shows where the plan stands.
"- Intelligence Network: task assignment exists only once mksk joins it. mkskj joins echo-net as @mksk (name/purpose:
"  g:inet_agents.mksk in vimpage_inet, optional). Then "assign dump_restore to memphia" records the agent and sends it
"  the target's brief, after your y.
"  Progress agents report to @mksk is staged and queued for you; the network never writes the file. The queued changes
"  show in the REVIEW pane right of the plan file (only while something waits): who reported it, the report, its edits
"  and its diff against the saved plan. There: y applies it, n drops it, v (or Enter) shows saved | with it side by side,
"  ]] / [[ jump between changes. ===p in the chat or mkskp goes to the pane. Applying waits for the running request;
"  the reporter is told the verdict.
"  An agent asking to give a target to an agent ("@mksk assign define_requirements to memphia") is queued the same way:
"  the pane shows the edits (agent column, "assigned" note) and "✉ y also sends @memphia the brief of ...". y saves it
"  and sends the brief; n drops it and nothing is sent. If that agent is off the network, y saves nothing and the
"  change stays with a warning: y again once it is back.
"- While mksk serves a network request (prompt badge QUEUE: what you type becomes your next request), it cannot ask you
"  anything: a "suggest" it tries is denied, and it decides from the plan or says what is unclear in its answer.
"- The plan functions are plain Lua (mksk_plan.lua): :lua require('mksk').plan.edit_target{target='cutover', status='WIP'}
"  then :MkskDiff and :lua require('mksk').plan.commit()  (or .discard()).
